# Handbook — The Rules | Canon 01-11
**Vault:** HakunaShortcut | Digital Frontier
**Status:** Battle-tested | Extracted in sequence
**Last Updated:** 24th August 2026
**Source:** Dispatches 001-011

> Knowledge is power. Systems are leverage. Ownership is resilience.

---

### Rule #1: The Data Bundle Rule
> Never let a single platform hold more than your next data bundle.

**Layer:** Liquidity
**Law:** Treat platforms as transaction pipes, not vaults.

### Rule #2: The Accumulation Rule
> Accumulate to dilute. Do not withdraw at minimum threshold when flat fees eat your capital.

**Layer:** Liquidity / Fees
**Law:** Flat fees punish small moves. Batch to protect margin.

### Rule #3: The Blind Platform Rule
> The platform isn't malicious. It's blind to the last mile. Your job is to see what it cannot.

**Layer:** Trust / Visibility
**Law:** No conspiracy needed. Limited context creates friction.

### Rule #4: The Signal Rule
> Dollars are not a product. Dollars are a signal — stop chasing capital, build the conditions that attract it.

**Layer:** Value / Trust
**Law:** Capital follows conditions, not requests.

### Rule #5: The Sentinel Rule
> Every gate has a sentinel. Every sentinel has incentives. Study the reason the lock was installed — not the lock itself.

**Layer:** Access / Control
**Law:** Understand incentive, not just obstacle.

### Rule #6: The Layer Rule
> Value explains why opportunity appears. Infrastructure determines where it flows. Locate your layer before you build your strategy.

**Layer:** Infrastructure
**Law:** Position before effort.

### Rule #7: The Borrowed Ground Rule
> Borrowed ground should never become permanent residence. The platform may introduce you. Ownership is what allows you to stay.

**Layer:** Ownership / Distribution
**Law:** Introduction ≠ residence.

### Rule #8: The Portability Rule
> Ownership protects your rights. Portability protects your continuity. An asset that cannot survive migration is not fully owned — it is parked on borrowed ground.

**Layer:** Ownership / Resilience
**Law:** If it can't move, you don't own it — you're parking.

### Rule #9: The Movement Rule
> Movement is universal. Infrastructure determines how far value can travel. Ownership determines who benefits when it arrives.

**Source:** Log 008
**Gate:** 03 - Movement
**Pattern:** Distribution compounds early: Stranger → Reader → Subscriber → Archive → Trust

### Rule #10: The Protocol Rule
> Do not optimize for the interface. Map the protocol. The dashboard tells you what happened. The architecture determines what becomes possible.

**Source:** Log 009
**Gate:** 03 - Movement
**Pattern:** Dashboard vs Protocol | Airport terminal ≠ Airport

### Rule #11: The Six Layers Rule
> Plug into the six layers — compute, payments, identity, distribution, trust, data — and effort compounds. Operate outside them, and you burn out against friction you can't see.

**Source:** Log 010
**Gate:** 04 - Architecture
**Stack:** Compute | Payments | Identity | Distribution | Trust | Data
**Modes:** Tenant (~1x) → Optimized (modest) → Operator (compounding)

